---
import Todo from '@/components/ui/Todo.astro';
import { site } from '@/data/site';
import CapabilityLayout from '@/layouts/CapabilityLayout.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'Do you stress-relieve every batch?',
    a: 'Yes. The furnace is in-house. Coiled springs go through it before dispatch.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do you grind every compression spring?',
    a: 'Only when the drawing asks for ground ends. Grinding is often skipped on the finest wire in our range.',
  },
];
---

<CapabilityLayout
  route="heatTreatment"
  title="Spring Stress Relieving & End Grinding"
  description="In-house stress-relieving furnace and end grinding for springs, in Talawade, Pune. Plating and other finishes through partners. Quote within 24 hours."
  h1="Stress relieving and end grinding"
  lede="Two in-house steps after the coil: the furnace, and the grinder when the drawing asks for flat ends. We do not plate here."
  context="a ground or stress-relieved spring"
  faqs={faqs}
  related={[
    {
      to: 'coilingForming',
      label: 'Spring coiling and forming',
      description: 'What happens before the furnace.',
    },
    {
      to: 'compression',
      label: 'Compression springs',
      description: 'Where ground ends are most often specified.',
    },
    {
      to: 'quality',
      label: 'Quality',
      description: 'ZED certification and how a new part is approved.',
    },
  ]}
>
  <h2>What it is</h2>
  <p>
    After coiling, residual stress sits in the wire. We take the batch through our{' '}
    <strong>stress-relieving furnace</strong>. That is a heat to relax the coil, not a
    quench-and-temper of the steel.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>End grinding</strong> flattens the last coil of a compression spring so it stands
    square. We have the machine. We use it when the drawing says closed-and-ground or
    open-and-ground.
  </p>
  <p>
    <Todo text="furnace and grinder details, and the smallest wire diameter you will grind." />
  </p>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <p>
    Coil and form → stress-relieve → grind ends if specified → finish through partners if specified
    → pack and dispatch ex-works Talawade.
  </p>
  <p>Plating, passivation and other coatings leave the building.</p>

  <h2>When to specify a grind</h2>
  <p>
    When the spring must sit flat and share the load around the last coil. Skip it on very fine wire
    unless you have checked with us — {site.capability.wireMinMm.toFixed(2)} mm is the bottom of the
    range, and a grind there is often more trouble than it is worth.
  </p>

  <h2>Limits</h2>
  <p>
    Wire {site.capability.wireRangeLabel}. No in-house plating. No lab numbers attached to the
    furnace cycle until we publish them.
  </p>
</CapabilityLayout>
